# The engine hands out a whole number of a list of doubles in the box of a double. A case of a switch takes it by its value, says that it is 3 and leaves the box. Every store of a boxed int32 brings it into the form of its type
# (ConversionEmitter::inFormOfType()), but the one in the typed copy of a loop did not: `3333333 0,0,0,0,0,0,0 -1 false [0,0,0,0,0,0,0] 0`, silent, and half right: a read through the stub hands the whole word back.
